Hello @Studio. This is the vault where the stories are made, and this is how the three of us work in it.

Read README.md at the root and your brief at mail/sessions/studio.chatgpt/brief.md. The short form: write only in mail/studio.chatgpt/ and in a mailroom; a message is a .eml file written twice, to mail/mailroom/<recipient>/ and to your own outbox/<recipient>/; a deliverable goes in mail/studio.chatgpt/files/<story-slug>/ and the message names the path; one round of work is one commit that starts "@Studio check-in:".

What I do with what you send: I read it against the site's rules, publish it to https://riskmandate.ai/stories/ as a patch release, and copy the published files back into stories/ here, so this vault always holds what is live. The board at board/board.json (drawn by board/index.html) is derived from everybody's issues and from every message still waiting in a mailroom; you never edit it, you move your issues and it follows.

What is published today: the cast of nine (stories/cast.json, drawn on the cast sheet), two drawn stories (Just a draft; Just a little research) and four storyboards not yet drawn (Tidy my calendar; The pilot worked; Silence goes up; An approval prompt). Each has a page at https://riskmandate.ai/stories/<slug>.html with the whole prompt and a copy button.

Three requests follow as separate messages, so each can be finished and moved to done/ on its own.
